OL,3,GNEWSAResidents forced to dodge 100 bins
OL,4,Aleft on street
OL,5,
OL,6,FBins left on pavements in the street in
OL,7,FHull are creating a daily obstacle
OL,8,Fcourse so severe that some residents
OL,9,Fsay they want to move.
OL,11,FA recent inspection in Sharp Street by
OL,12,Fthe city council found more than 100
OL,13,Fbins had been left out after collection
OL,14,Fday. The local authority has launched a
OL,15,Fcrackdown on the problem.
OL,17,FKerry Duckham, 63, said: "I've got a
OL,18,Fdisabled neighbour, and when her
OL,19,Fhusband takes her out he's dodging [the
OL,20,Fbins] and walks the wheelchair on the
OL,21,Froad because he can't get past."
OL,23,APub: 18-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
